---
import Layout from '@boring-sites/design/Layout.astro';
import NoLogsBanner from '../components/NoLogsBanner.astro';
const siteName = 'What Is My IP';
---
<Layout
  title="Terms of Service"
  description="Terms of service for What Is My IP."
  siteName={siteName}
>
  <NoLogsBanner />
  <article class="container-prose py-12">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold">Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-neutral-500">Last updated: 2026-08-18</p>

    <div class="prose mt-8 dark:prose-invert">
      <h2>Acceptance</h2>
      <p>By using What Is My IP, you agree to these terms. If you don't agree, don't use the site.</p>

      <h2>What this site is</h2>
      <p>A free utility that displays your public IP address and runs a few diagnostic checks. We provide it as-is, with no warranty of any kind. We try to keep it accurate and available, but we can't guarantee it.</p>

      <h2>What you agree not to do</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Don't use the site to harm anyone or break any law.</li>
        <li>Don't try to break the site (DDoS, scraping at scale, exploit hunting) without permission.</li>
        <li>Don't rely on this site for security-critical decisions. Use a dedicated security tool.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>No security guarantees</h2>
      <p>
        The DNS leak and WebRTC leak tests are heuristics, not definitive. They are useful for casual checks, not for verifying that a VPN is working correctly. For security-critical verification, use a dedicated tool like ipleak.net or browserleaks.com.
      </p>

      <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>What Is My IP is provided "as is" without warranty. We are not liable for any damages arising from your use of the site.</p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>We may update these terms. Material changes will be noted on the home page.</p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions? Email us at <a href="mailto:hello@whatismyip.example.com">hello@whatismyip.example.com</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
